# media/plotly.min.js is a verbatim upstream artifact whose sha256 is pinned in
# deps.json. Git sees minified JS as text, so under core.autocrlf=true (the
# Windows default) checkout rewrote its 3881 LFs to CRLF -- a 4855045-byte file
# where upstream shipped 4851164, with a different hash. The stored blob was
# always correct; only the working copy was mangled, which meant every fresh
# clone on Windows failed `npm run fetch-vendor -- --check` and packaged a
# byte-modified plotly into the .vsix. Marking it binary stops all conversion.
media/plotly.min.js binary

# Same reasoning for anything else that must survive byte-exact.
*.vsix binary
*.tar.gz binary
*.ttf binary
*.pfb binary
